    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\r\n\r\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\r\n\r\n### Module(s)\r\n\r\nmini.trailspace\r\n\r\n### Description\r\n\r\nI want to disable trailing space highlighting in [lspsaga](https://github.com/glepnir/lspsaga.nvim)'s finder window (`LspSaga lsp_finder` command)\r\n\r\n![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/5768792/217278750-cc2011e9-e22f-4115-8daf-478654e5c26a.png)\r\n\r\nWhat I have in my config (using `lazy.nvim`):\r\n```lua\r\n{\r\n  'echasnovski/mini.trailspace',\r\n  event = 'BufReadPost',\r\n  opts = {\r\n    blacklist = {\r\n      'lspsagafinder',\r\n    },\r\n  },\r\n  config = function(_, opts)\r\n    vim.api.nvim_create_autocmd('FileType', {\r\n      pattern = opts.blacklist,\r\n      callback = function()\r\n        vim.b.minitrailspace_disable = true\r\n        MiniTrailspace.unhighlight() -- force an update?\r\n      end,\r\n    })\r\n\r\n    require('mini.trailspace').setup()\r\n  end,\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nIf I manually call `:lua MiniTrailspace.unhighlight()`, the whitespace highlighting will be disabled\r\n\r\n### Neovim version\r\n\r\n0.8.3\r\n\r\n### Steps to reproduce\r\n\r\nSorry, since my issue requires LSP and other stuff, I didn't create a minimal config. Let me know if that's necessary and I can try creating one\r\n\r\n### Expected behavior\r\n\r\nI expect the highlighting to be disabled in the `lspsagafinder` file type (when I do `:set ft?` in that window, that's the filetype I get\r\n\r\n### Actual behavior\r\n\r\nThe spaces keep being highlighted",
