        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "I believe the reason is how 'lspsaga' creates those \"lsp_finder\" windows. See more in [this comment](https://github.com/glepnir/lspsaga.nvim/issues/844#issuecomment-1421124170). And one more piece to this puzzle: 'mini.trailspace' calls `highlight()` on every `WinEnter` and it *should* unhighlight in target window (as `vim.b.minitrailspace_disable` is indeed set in correct buffer), but the ever giving problem here is that `WinEnter` is not triggered for floating windows.\r\n\r\nI managed to workaround this issue by using `vim.schedule(MiniTrailspace.unhighlight)` instead of directly calling `MiniTrailspace.unhighlight()` inside autocommand callback.\r\n\r\nDoes this solve it for you?",
