        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> > I managed to workaround this issue by using `vim.schedule(MiniTrailspace.unhighlight)`\r\n> \r\n> Yes @echasnovski , that does solve the issue it seems\r\n> \r\n> Just wondering: if we do this, do we still need to set `vim.b.minitrailspace_disable` or it doesn't matter anymore?\r\n\r\nIf you want to state that this buffer shouldn't highlighted trailing whitespace, you should set it. Otherwise, at least in theory, you can rehighlight. In practice, it probably won't happen, as it seems that [target events](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/lua/mini/trailspace.lua#L69) won't get triggered in that buffer.\r\n\r\nClosing this then, as it doesn't seem to really be a 'mini.trailspace' problem (at least for now).",
